.TH "DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTUREEVENT.DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTUREEVENT" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DocumentPictureInPictureEvent.DocumentPictureInPictureEvent \-
DocumentPictureInPictureEvent: DocumentPictureInPictureEvent()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]DocumentPictureInPictureEvent()\f[B]\f[R] constructor
creates a new \f[CR]DocumentPictureInPictureEvent\f[R] object instance.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new DocumentPictureInPictureEvent(type, init)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
A string representing the type of event.
In the case of \f[CR]DocumentPictureInPictureEvent\f[R] this is always
\f[CR]enter\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]init\f[R]
An object containing the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]window\f[R]
A \f[CR]Window\f[R] instance representing the browsing context inside
the \f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[R] window the event was fired on.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
A developer would not use this constructor manually.
A new \f[CR]DocumentPictureInPictureEvent\f[R] object is constructed
when a handler is invoked as a result of the \f[CR]enter\f[R] event
firing.
.IP
.EX
documentPictureInPicture.addEventListener(\(dqenter\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] pipWindow = event.window;
  console.log(\(dqVideo player has entered the pip window\(dq);

  \f[B]const\f[R] pipMuteButton = pipWindow.document.createElement(\(dqbutton\(dq);
  pipMuteButton.textContent = \(dqMute\(dq;
  pipMuteButton.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]const\f[R] pipVideo = pipWindow.document.querySelector(\(dq#video\(dq);
    \f[B]if\f[R] (!pipVideo.muted) {
      pipVideo.muted = \f[B]true\f[R];
      pipMuteButton.textContent = \(dqUnmute\(dq;
    } \f[B]else\f[R] {
      pipVideo.muted = \f[B]false\f[R];
      pipMuteButton.textContent = \(dqMute\(dq;
    }
  });

  pipWindow.document.body.append(pipMuteButton);
});
.EE
